# OPERATIONS §2.3 (M3): the refused scenario files' lines print "in full-path order" (E §3.1 step 1), not by the
# scenarios' ids: a.tally holds zeta and b.tally holds alpha, each refused for an id the base declares (LOAD-DUP),
# so zeta's line comes first; then the warning load decides (s cited by nothing). (run prints the same two lines,
# by id, before its results.) Exit 1.
=== options check exit=1
=== m.tally
model f
  tally 2
  on 2025-01-01
  start 2025-01-01
  end 2025-12-31
source s "synthetic"
unit DUK: currency minor 0.01
ask q: minor(DUK)
=== b.tally
scenario alpha over f
  tally 2
  from 2025-01-01
def q: int = 1
ask qa: q in alpha
=== a.tally
scenario zeta over f
  tally 2
  from 2025-01-01
def q: int = 2
ask qz: q in zeta
=== expect
scenario zeta: refused: LOAD-DUP q is declared twice (a.tally:4)
scenario alpha: refused: LOAD-DUP q is declared twice (b.tally:4)
warning: WARN-UNREAD source s is read by nothing
